	(text "Board notes\n * 90 x 70 mm, 4 x M2 holes 2 mm from the corners: drop-in for the perfboard (cad CustomBoard).\n * OSH Park 4-layer: L1 signal / L2 GND plane / L3 +5V plane / L4 signal.\n   Rules: 5/5 mil track/space, 10 mil drill, 4 mil ring, 15 mil edge keep-out.\n * Teensy 4.1 and ESP32 sit on female sockets. R1-R7, D1, D2, Q1 are under the Teensy;\n   U5, C2, R8-R12 under the ESP32: seat them flat (keep them under ~7 mm).\n * 3.3 V rails stay split, never tied: +3V3_TEENSY (Teensy regulator) feeds IMU logic, CAN\n   modules, UART6/7, I2C; +3V3_ESP32 (DevKit regulator) feeds TFT and lasers.\n * D1 feeds Teensy VIN from +5V, so Teensy USB cannot back-feed the 5 V rail (VUSB-VIN pad\n   can stay uncut). ESP32 USB still back-feeds +5V through the DevKit's own diode.\n * No copper pour / vias under the ESP32 antenna (rule area on the PCB).\n * PCB status: routed 2026-10-08 (Freerouting 2.5.0, KiCad DRC clean). Re-route a connector if its pin order changes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.36 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "124d66f5-adf4-4a8f-a46f-f6bea57fe708")
	)
