	)
	(text "TEENSY 4.1  (control, CAN, IMU, RC)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(thickness 0.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6456061a-b15c-4501-b09f-f31f23d68c39")
	)
	(text "Connector pin orders copy the existing perfboard cables (photo, sketch and answers of 2026-10-07).\nCheck each one against the real cable / module before routing. Physical order on the board:\n   J1   BUZZER       top edge, left->right: BZ-, BZ+\n   J2   RGB_LED      left edge, top->bottom: B, G, GND, R\n   J3   ELRS_RX      left edge, top->bottom: GND, 5V, RX (->Teensy 16), TX (Teensy 17->)\n   J4   IMU_SIG      left edge, top->bottom: RST, INT, CS, AD0, SDA, SCL\n   J5   IMU_PWR      left edge, top->bottom: GND, VCC (+5V)\n   J6   AK45_UART2   bottom edge (inner row), left->right: GND, TX (Teensy 14), RX (Teensy 15)\n   J7   AK45_UART1   bottom edge (outer row), left->right: GND, TX (Teensy 8), RX (Teensy 7)\n   J8   AK45_CAN     bottom edge, left->right: CANH, CANL\n   J9   ODRIVE_CAN   bottom edge, left->right: GND, CANH, CANL\n   J10  5V_IN        bottom edge, left->right: GND, +5V\n   J11  LASER1       bottom edge (outer row), left->right: XSHUT, INT, SDA, SCL, GND, 3V3\n   J12  LASER2       bottom edge (outer row), left->right: XSHUT, INT, SDA, SCL, GND, 3V3\n   J13  LASER3       bottom edge (inner row), left->right: XSHUT, INT, SDA, SCL, GND, 3V3\n   J14  LASER4       bottom edge (inner row), left->right: XSHUT, INT, SDA, SCL, GND, 3V3\n   J15  TFT_PWR      right edge, top->bottom: GND, 3V3\n   J16  TFT_SIG      right edge, top->bottom: SCL, SDA, RST, DC, CS, BL\n   J17  NEOPIXEL     right edge, top->bottom: 5V, GND, DATA\n   J18  LIMIT_L      new: right edge, top->bottom: GND, SIG (Teensy 23)\n   J19  LIMIT_R      new: right edge, top->bottom: GND, SIG (Teensy 22)\n   J20  UART6        new: inner column, top->bottom: TX (Teensy 24), RX (Teensy 25), 3V3, GND\n   J21  UART7        new: inner column, top->bottom: RX (Teensy 28), TX (Teensy 29), 3V3, GND\n   J22  I2C          new: inner column, top->bottom: SCL (Teensy 19), SDA (Teensy 18), 3V3, GND\n   J23  TEENSY_GPIO  new: 2.54 mm header, top->bottom: 3V3, 26, 27, 32, GND, 41..33 (beside the Teensy pins)\n   J24  ESP32_GPIO   new: 2.54 mm header, top->bottom: GND, 3V3, IO19, IO32, IO33\n\nSpecific doubts:\n * IMU J5: VCC is +5V (as told) - the BNO08x module must have its own 3.3 V regulator.\n * IMU SPI: module SDA -> Teensy 12 (MISO), AD0 -> Teensy 11 (MOSI), SCL -> Teensy 13 (SCK), per the\n   BNO08x datasheet (H_SDA/H_MISO, SA0/H_MOSI). pinout.MD listed SDA/AD0 the other way round:\n   verify against the working perfboard before routing.\n * ELRS J3: RX / TX are named from the TEENSY side (RX = receiver TX into Teensy 16) - assumed,\n   same convention as the AK45 UARTs (confirmed).\n * CAN modules U3/U4: single row 3V3 GND CTX CRX CANH CANL. This board is one end of each bus:\n   check whether the HiLetgo module has a 120R terminator fitted.\n * Every JST-XH header: latch side faces the board centre, as on the perfboard. Pin 1 = square pad.\n * LASER1..4 = firmware sensors 0..3: XSHUT GPIO14/27/26/25, INT GPIO34/35/36/39.\n * The back silkscreen prints every connector pin name: compare it with the cables."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 200 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "718b99e6-8b63-4881-abc8-6af142a5b809")
	)
